<!--
	Kitsune Shugyo settings: how fast crafting skills and attributes level.

	preset = SLOW, MEDIUM or FAST

	                         SLOW   MEDIUM   FAST
	  weapon   kills            16      12      4   (kills holding that weapon type)
	  tool     hits             80      60     20   (block hits / repairs with that tool)
	  use      uses              8       6      2   (food and medical items consumed)
	  craft    items             8       6      2   (items crafted, per skill)
	  station  completions      16       8      4   (any workstation queue, campfire included)
	  vehicle  repairs           4       2      1   (vehicle repairs with a repair kit)
	  wire     connections       4       2      1   (wire tool connections)
	  loot     containers       30      20      8   (fresh loot containers opened; Backpacks skill)
	  wreck    hits             80      60     20   (salvage-tool hits on vehicle wrecks; Vehicles skill)
	  attribute points          40      25     10   (attributes; see below)

	Each number is how many of that action earn +1 level. HIGHER = SLOWER.
	SLOW is roughly double the vanilla magazine grind, FAST roughly half.
	Every source fills the same bar, so 40 salvage hits plus two magazines
	are one Salvage Tools level on SLOW.

	To fine-tune, add any of the names above as an attribute and it
	overrides the preset for that one source. Example: MEDIUM, but
	weapons level twice as slowly:

	  <KitsuneShugyo preset="MEDIUM" weapon="24" />

	Attributes (Perception, Strength, Fortitude, Agility, Intellect) are
	earned by practice, not bought with skill points; skill points buy perks
	only. `attribute` is practice points per rank step: going from rank r to
	r+1 costs r x attribute points. A kill with gear tagged for that
	attribute is 1 point (rifles: Perception, clubs: Strength, ...), so on
	SLOW, rank 1 -> 2 is 40 kills and rank 9 -> 10 is 360. Other sources
	(block hits, upgrades, injuries healed, sneak attacks, looting,
	crafting, reading, trading) are listed in the README.

	Magazines are back in loot and on traders, at vanilla rates. Reading one
	adds part of a level to its skill instead of a whole level:

	  magazine   levels per read, default 0.25 (a quarter of a level).
	             Any number above 0 and up to 10; 1 = vanilla.

	  share      party (default): a magazine or perk book you read also
	             teaches everyone in your party, wherever they are.
	             nearby: only party members within `range` metres
	             (default 100).
	             off: nobody shares.

	  <KitsuneShugyo preset="SLOW" magazine="0.5" share="off" />

	Anti-grind: practice tires an attribute. After `fatigue` practice points
	(default 60, about 60 walker kills) in a short time, that attribute
	learns at a quarter until it rests; it recovers fully in `rest` in-game
	hours (default 6). fatigue="0" turns this off. Crafting skills don't tire.

	  <KitsuneShugyo preset="SLOW" fatigue="100" rest="4" share="nearby" range="150" />

	Skill points (optional): attributes are earned by practice, so skill
	points only buy perks and can pile up late in a game. points_after is a
	player level (default 0 = off); past it, a skill point comes only every
	points_every levels (default 2).

	  <KitsuneShugyo preset="SLOW" points_after="100" points_every="2" />

	Multiplayer: only the SERVER's copy of this file counts. It is baked into
	the config the server sends every player. Restart the server after editing.

	Single player: takes effect the next time you load a world.

	Existing characters pick up the new pace on their next login; progress
	already earned toward the next level is kept. If this file is missing or
	unreadable, the mod falls back to SLOW, 0.25 and party.
-->
<KitsuneShugyo preset="SLOW" magazine="0.25" share="party" />
